+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"ee6df0a7-5193-481e-b806-cf5b705cf8dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan the implementation.\n\nThe project is set up with:\n- TypeScript with ES2022/Node16 modules\n- Express, ws, better-sqlite3 already installed\n- A schema.sql file with documents, versions, and active_connections tables\n- Entry point requirement: `src/server.ts` exporting `createApp` factory function\n\nI need to implement:\n\n1. **Database layer** - SQLite with better-sqlite3, using the schema\n2. **REST API** - Express routes for CRUD on documents + version history\n3. **WebSocket handler** - Real-time collaboration with ws\n4. **Operational Transform** - OT for conflict resolution\n5. **Server factory** - `createApp` function that returns `{ app, start, stop }`\n\nLet me think about the Operational Transform approach:\n\nFor a simple text-based OT, I'll implement:\n- Operations: insert (position, text) and delete (position, length)\n- Transform function: When two concurrent operations happen, transform one against the other so both are preserved\n- Version tracking: Each document has a version number that increments with each operation\n\nThe key OT transform rules for text:\n- insert(a) vs insert(b) at same position: one goes before the other (e.g., by client ID)\n- insert(a) at pos P vs delete(b) from pos P: adjust positions\n- delete(a) vs delete(b) overlapping: adjust ranges\n\nLet me design the data structures:\n\n```typescript\ntype Operation = \n  | { type: 'insert'; pos: number; text: string; clientId: string }\n  | { type: 'delete'; pos: number; length: number; clientId: string };\n\n// Message types (client -> server):\n// { type: 'join', docId: string }\n// { type: 'operation', op: Operation, version: number }\n// { type: 'cursor', pos: number }\n\n// Message types (server -> client):\n// { type: 'sync', content: st